      en: "When given large sums, he would distribute them completely the same day — keeping nothing. Once, when 70,000 dirhams arrived in Medina, he distributed all of them before sunset. Aisha ر reported he never had more than a handful of dates in the house. But — crucially — he never worried about money. He trusted Allah for provision completely. He said: 'If you trusted Allah as He deserves to be trusted, He would provide for you as He provides for the birds — they leave in the morning empty and return full.'",
